@startuml escalation_state_machine
title OIOF — Escalation State Machine

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #4A5568
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F7FAFC
  BorderColor #4A5568
  FontColor #1A202C
}

state "Decision Pending" as DecisionPending

[*] --> Detected : alert threshold breach\nor manual report

Detected --> Triaged : deterministic evidence\ncollection + validation complete

Triaged --> Investigating : Orchestrator analysis (Prompt 01)\n+ Independent challenge (Prompt 02)\nunderway

Investigating --> DecisionPending : Decision Matrix drafted,\nawaiting named human owner(s)

DecisionPending --> Contained : decision(s) approved\nand executed

Contained --> Monitoring : reversible actions in place,\nauth-rate trend re-checked

state "Closure Pending" as ClosurePending
Monitoring --> ClosurePending : deterministic closure criteria met:\nauth rate within 1pt of baseline for 2+ consecutive hours,\nall Decision Matrix rows terminal, and review scheduled
ClosurePending --> Resolved : Incident Commander explicitly\napproves closure
ClosurePending --> Investigating : Incident Commander rejects closure\nor new evidence arrives

Monitoring --> Investigating : new evidence contradicts\ncurrent hypothesis set

Resolved --> Review : begin scheduled post-incident review

Review --> [*]

Triaged --> Escalated : severity re-assessed upward
Investigating --> Escalated : approval deadline passed\nwithout decision
DecisionPending --> Escalated : customer_risk = high OR\nreversibility = low
Escalated --> DecisionPending : Incident Commander +\nExecutive Sponsor engaged

note right of Escalated
  Escalation never resolves itself
  automatically. A human (Incident
  Commander or Executive Sponsor)
  must act to leave this state.
end note

note bottom of Resolved
  Closure criteria per PROC-001.
  Always a human (Incident
  Commander) decision — never
  automatic.
end note

@enduml
